 "answer": "If by **KL** you mean **Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia: yes, I’d plan to stay indoors for now**, especially for exercise. It’s just after midnight on **Sunday, October 18**, local time. The latest city reading I could verify was **AQI 155 (“Unhealthy”) at 10 p.m. Saturday**—not a reading for the rest of Sunday. Malaysia’s health ministry advises people with asthma to avoid going out during haze when air pollution is elevated. ([aqicn.org](https://aqicn.org/city/kuala-lumpur/))\n\n**Check the reading for your part of KL again before going out later today.** If it remains high, keep windows closed, use filtered air if available, and carry your reliever inhaler. If you’re wheezing or short of breath, follow your asthma action plan; seek urgent care if symptoms are severe or aren’t improving with your prescribed reliever. ([infosihat.moh.gov.my](https://infosihat.moh.gov.my/images/isusemasa/Jerebu/04_Jerebu%2009%20BI.pdf?utm_source=openai))",
